## root-cause (USE PUBLIC DATA SOURCES, 04/11 12:10) — no hand-maintained model list
Catalogue = merge of (1) OpenRouter public GET https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models (keyless; ids, context, pricing) and (2) LiteLLM https://raw.githubusercontent.com/BerriAI/litellm/main/model_prices_and_context_window.json (fills gaps), plus our own live /models per configured provider. Tolerate either source failing (keep last good snapshot), refresh on a schedule. Pattern reference: lean-ctx live_pricing.rs (OpenRouter first, LiteLLM fills gaps). No model ids or scores hard-coded in code (scripts/ai/check-no-hardcode.mjs must pass).

## root-cause (SCORING, 04/11 12:40) — fold into TASK-AI-166, no new Work Item
WHERE: tools/ai-brain/priors.js normalisation (normalizedScore per benchmark; FALLBACK_BENCHMARKS = ['aggregate','benchlm']).
WRONG: a model scored only by the fallback aggregate gets its BenchLM percentile as its score, so it outranks multi-source models: deepseek-v4-1-flash raw 65.2 -> 97.1 (above claude-opus-5-5 95.3, raw 86.9); dots-3-note-preview 96.7; glm-5 91. Writers are then chosen on inflated numbers.
GOAL: scores comparable across models. Either (a) map fallback-only models onto the primary (Artificial Analysis coding/agentic) scale using the models present in BOTH sources (fitted from data each refresh, nothing typed by hand), or (b) keep their rawScore and mark them provisional so routing ranks them below any multi-source model with a higher raw score. Free/preview variants (":free", "-free", "-preview") must not inherit the full model's score without their own evidence; use measured outcomes (commit rate / first-review PASS from the pipeline metrics) when available.
VERIFY: test: a fallback-only model with raw 65 never outranks a multi-source model with raw 86; deepseek-v4-1-flash < claude-opus-5-5 after refresh; node scripts/ai/check-no-hardcode.mjs passes.
